{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789592378,"nonce":"cX4MLWthroYRcISS4uQbxSLPpp4=","title":"b4 trailers: comma in From: name accepts any follow-up trailer","message":"`LoreMessage.get_trailers()` drops a follow-up person trailer whose address and\nname do not match the sender's. When the sender's `From:` name contains a\ncomma, the name check always succeeds, so every person trailer in that reply is\naccepted regardless of who it names.\n\nReproducer\n----------\n\n```python\n\u003e\u003e\u003e check('Bob Smith \u003cbob@example.com\u003e', 'Reviewed-by: Alice Jones \u003calice@example.com\u003e')\n    accepted: []\n    mismatch: ['Reviewed-by: Alice Jones \u003calice@example.com\u003e']\n\u003e\u003e\u003e check('\"Smith, Bob\" \u003cbob@example.com\u003e', 'Reviewed-by: Alice Jones \u003calice@example.com\u003e')\n    accepted: ['Reviewed-by: Alice Jones \u003calice@example.com\u003e']\n    mismatch: []\n```\n\nSame trailer, same non-matching identity; only the sender's display name\ndiffers. Expected: both land in `mismatch`.\n\nRoot cause\n----------\n\n`src/b4/__init__.py:1955-1962`, the comma branch of the name comparison:\n\n```python\nelif hlname.find(',') \u003e 0:\n    nmatch = True\n    for nchunk in hlname.split(','):\n        if hlname.find(nchunk.strip()) \u003c 0:\n            nmatch = False\n            break\n```\n\n`hlname` is the sender's name (`self.fromname.lower()`, line 1948) and `tlname`\nis the trailer's name (`ltr.addr[0].lower()`, line 1947). The branch splits\n`hlname` into chunks and then searches for each chunk in `hlname` — the same\nstring it split. Every chunk is by construction a substring of it, so the loop\ncan never clear `nmatch`, which was set to `True` on entry at line 1956.\n\n`nmatch` is therefore `True` for any sender whose name contains a comma, and\nline 1964 appends the trailer to the accepted list. `tlname` is read at line\n1947 but never used in this branch.\n\nScope\n-----\n\nOnly reached when the address comparison has already failed\n(`ltr.email_eq(self.fromemail)`, line 1939) and the names are not equal\n(line 1950), and only for trailers with `type == 'person'` and a parsed\n`addr` (line 1936). `sloppy=True` bypasses the whole check earlier and is\nunaffected.\n\nThe comma form is what a `From:` of `\"Lastname, Firstname\" \u003caddr\u003e` produces, a\nshape several corporate mail systems emit, so the affected senders are a real\npopulation rather than a corner case.","files":null}]}